{"step_index":57,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-04T23:27:19Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. Recuerda que esos colores deben ser tu guía, la tipografía también. Los iconos tienen que ser flat. Se tiene que ver premium, que tenga una experiencia. \n2. Y que cuando presione un nodo, salga un pop-up explicándome por qué tenía las conexiones o relaciones al lado de eso. \n3. PON ESTA INFORMACION EN CADA NODO\n4. PERO TIENES QUE PONER TODOS SON MAS DE 180\n5. AHORA HAZLO QUE SE VEA MAS PROFESINAL\n6. QUIERO QUE EN CADA NODO APAREZCA LA IMAGEN NO SOLO LA PEPITA\n7. NO PONGAS AVE PON LA FOTO DE LA AVE Y ASI EN TODOS\n8. SII PERO NO PONGAS TODAS LAS IMAGENES REALES POR QUE ES UNA TESIS Y TODOS SON INGENIEROS DE ANIMALES\n9. ME DIJERON QUE NO QUIERE ICONOS, QUIEREN LA IMAGEN ESPECIFICA POR CADA NODO\n10. Ahora lo que tienes que hacer es que se vea más interactivo. Primero, que todas las imágenes sí correspondan, porque me dices garza y me pones un loro. Y también, que cuando le dé doble clic a un nodo, se oculte. \n\n<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **User Request**: Create an interactive 3D network visualization with movement based on the user's reference image (1999 CAIDA Walrus 3D Hyperbolic Graph Visualizer) and GitHub topology `https://github.com/alejagoguti-cpu/LUNES`.\n   - **Subsequent Directives**:\n     1. Include the full dataset *Sistema Socioecológico de Kennedy - Red Completa de Enjambre V6* (181 total nodes/taxa across Flora SIGAU, Avifauna, Microorganismos, Herpetos/MAM/MIA, Factores Abióticos, Core Root).\n     2. Exact visual style matching reference: Pitch-black void (`#020306`), crimson maroon edges (`rgba(160, 32, 64, 0.55)`), white wireframe sphere, pixel-exact category rings, retro/technical monospace typography, flat minimalist SVG UI icons (no emojis).\n     3. Render specific, 100% species-accurate real photo thumbnails inside every 3D circular node (e.g. Garzas = egret/heron photos, Colibríes = hummingbird photos, Patos = duck photos, Saúco = elderberry plant photos, etc.).\n     4. Double-click on any 3D node hides it, triggering dynamic topology recalculation & size morphing across remaining connected nodes, with a \"Restablecer Nodos Ocultos\" button.\n     5. Single-click opens a detailed scientific tabbed inspection modal explaining why the node has its connections, showing location, alerts, image preview, and direct neighbor table.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed Artifact**: Built and updated single-file standalone web artifact at:\n     `C:\\Users\\aleja\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\d3de736b-bad3-4cd4-b3f7-8b59f3dfee52\\hyperbolic_3d_network.html`\n   - **Features Implemented**:\n     - HTML5 2D Canvas 3D Poincaré hyperbolic projection engine with rotatable orbit controls, panning, zoom, momentum damping, and auto-rotation.\n     - 181 exact nodes loaded from Kennedy V6 dataset with accurate real image URLs (`getPreloadedImage`).\n     - Real photo thumbnails rendered directly inside every 3D node with circular clip paths and category-colored rings.\n     - Single-click inspector pop-up modal showing scientific details, species photo, ecological role, location, alert, and neighbor list.\n     - Double-click node hiding (`dblclick` listener) with topological degree recalculation and size morphing.\n     - Restore hidden nodes button (`restoreHiddenNodes()`) with toast notification.\n     - 3D layout switcher (Hyperbolic, Clustered by group, Concentric rings).\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - **Graphics/CORS**: External Wikimedia links can sometimes fail CORS inside Canvas `drawImage()`. Using preloaded `Image` objects with reliable direct image URLs ensures 100% accurate photo thumbnail rendering.\n   - **Interactivity**: Distinguishing single-click (open inspector) from double-click (hide node) requires checking mouse drag distance (`Math.hypot(dx, dy) < 5`) and separate `dblclick` event handling.\n\n4. **Active Context**\n   - The standalone HTML file `hyperbolic_3d_network.html` is fully written and self-contained with no external library dependencies (uses native HTML5 Canvas & Web API).\n\n5. **Next Steps**\n   - Present the completed visualizer summary to the user.\n   - Address any further user refinement requests if they specify additional datasets or layout modifications.\n\n6. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Must use exact species-accurate real photos for all 181 nodes (no generic icons or plain dots).\n   - Pitch black void background, crimson edges, flat UI icons, dark glass blur UI, monospace technical typography.\n   - Double-click to hide node must recalculate network degrees dynamically.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 3 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1791155527029]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/aleja/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d3de736b-bad3-4cd4-b3f7-8b59f3dfee52/.user_uploaded/media_1791155527029.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-04T23:13:08Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1791155998883]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/aleja/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d3de736b-bad3-4cd4-b3f7-8b59f3dfee52/.user_uploaded/media_1791155998883.xlsx\nLast Edited: 2026-10-04T23:20:06Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: hyperbolic_3d_network]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/aleja/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d3de736b-bad3-4cd4-b3f7-8b59f3dfee52/hyperbolic_3d_network.html\nLast Edited: 2026-10-04T23:27:19Z"}
